 football club  themselves these children are going to  get a warm scottish welcome scottish  hospitality and fully supported for all  the time that they need to be here  before it's safe for them to return to  ukraine  anecdotally i've seen plenty of reports  that there are any number of orphans in  ukraine at the moment it appears to be a  bit of an issue do we have any rough  idea of kind of how many there are there  that are still needing to be brought out  of the country well i mean there have  been various reports but i think the  figure that has been used has been a  figure as many as 10 000.  um i think you know one of the important  things is we're doing this today and i'm  really grateful to the likes of lord  harrington and kevin foster that have  helped us over the course of the last  few days but we're debating a bill  tomorrow that will criminalize refugees  and i want to say to conservative mps  just think about this just think about  the humanity that we're all showing  today let's make sure that we all of us  we all do our bit to make sure that we  welcome vulnerable people we did this  before the second world war with the  kinder transport that people often talk  about let's make sure that that  generosity that welcome  that sanctuary that people need at a  time such as this is something that we  can all be proud of so does this all  mean that you'll be doing a david  cameron then and popping yourself behind  the wheel and heading out there to the  front line or close to the front line  well look it's not it's not about me or  anyone else i think really we've got to  do what we can to to help and i think  myself my colleagues lots of other  people will want to do that but most  importantly it's about being a voice for  those that needed help being a voice to  help the the charity the neighbor kids  charity in this case but let's make sure  this is not the end of it but this is  the beginning of it and then we continue  to support those that neither we are  we're all watching the horrors unfolding  we've seen what's happening in mario  paul which is just just devastating to  see what's going on  we need to make sure there are safe  routes out for young people for families  that need our support i i suspect given  your position you're on the opposition  benches you're not in government but i  suspect your position means that you  might feel slightly freer than that the  health secretary was on the program this  morning we have now heard from a number  of very senior officials well senior  figures within ukraine senior figures  outside of ukraine that vladimir putin  is a war criminal and the acts of  genocide are being committed you can  feel comfortable saying well one of the  things i actually raised at prime  minister's questions a few weeks ago  that we need to change our own law to  reflect on acts of aggression i mean  it's clear that we need to go after the  perpetrators of these crimes there are  legal niceties in terms of the  definition of genocide these are  unspeakable crimes for a man that's  slaughtering innocent civilians in  ukraine that's all we need to know and  this man and his regime  need to be held to account but let's to  conclude let's talk about the orphans  that are coming across and like you do  not have to be a parent to to look at  the scenes you know in mario paul and  elsewhere where babies bodies are being  pulled from the rubble you don't have to  be a parent to find that morally  important but i suspect that there will  be plenty of parents  who would wish to help those children  that aren't lucky enough to have parents  how can they well i think people can  obviously register through the uk  government site and of course they can  tick the box if they're in scotland for  the  the super sponsors people want to do  this people want to help government  needs to make sure it can move at pace  we're facing war in europe  none of us ever thought we'd be seeing  this seeing europeans are being bombed  people are having to flee war  we need to do all that we can and we  need to make sure that we get people  should we have seen it should we have  seen it given what given what happened  to 2014 and even before  should we not have seen this coming i  think there have been  policy failures over the course of the  the last few years of course they are  but we are where we are now we need to  make sure that we're supporting the  ukrainians to the fullest extent with  the military support that's been given  to them that needs to go as far and as  fast as we can the humanitarian support  what counts today is the ukrainian  people and the way that they're  suffering from the bombardment of their  country  well we wish you the best of luck with  the kids coming across and maybe speak  to you once they've settled in up in  edinburgh for now in blackburn thanks  for joining us thank you
 

